      "title": "Token Service: Diagnosing HTTP 403 and Scope/Consent Mismatches",
      "content_summary": "Troubleshooting guide for resolving authorization errors and scope mismatches in the Token Service, focusing on permission validation and tenant isolation.",
      "content_body": "When encountering HTTP 403 errors or unexpected 'access denied' responses, first verify that the requested scopes align with the granted permissions in the token payload. Scope/consent mismatches often occur when a client application requests broader access than the user or admin has authorized. To resolve incorrect data visibility or wrong tenant data display, check the conditional access policies and ensure proper tenant isolation is enforced. If permissions are granted incorrectly, review recent policy changes and correct any operator errors in the role assignments. Completing a formal access review can help identify and rectify improper permissions that allow users to see data they shouldn't."
